# Team AX: grow the data filesystem online when ax-hostd resizes the data zvol (resizeTenant, isolation.md §5.7).
# The kernel sends a "change" uevent with the new capacity; resize2fs is a no-op when the size did not change.
# Run outside udev (systemd-run) so a long resize is not killed by the udev worker timeout.
ACTION=="change", SUBSYSTEM=="block", ENV{ID_FS_LABEL}=="axdata", ENV{ID_FS_TYPE}=="ext4", RUN+="/usr/bin/systemd-run --no-block --collect --unit=ax-axdata-resize /usr/sbin/resize2fs $devnode"
